-- title:
--   Finite faithful flatness over a subalgebra with reduced fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that the image of $p$ in $\mathcal O$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly the principal ideal $(p)$, and assume $\mathcal O$ is complete and separated for the $(p)$-adic topology. Let $H$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module and whose fibre $\mathbb Z/p \otimes_{\mathcal O} H$ is a reduced ring, let $T$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is likewise free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, and let $\iota \colon H \to T$ be an injective homomorphism of $\mathcal O$-algebras. Then the ring homomorphism underlying $\iota$ is finite, i.e. $T$ is a finitely generated $H$-module, and faithfully flat. No nontriviality of $H$ or $T$ is assumed, and $T$ is not required to have reduced fibre.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra form of the assertion that, for a finite flat group scheme $G$ over $\mathbb Z_p$, the quotient map $G \to G^{\mathrm{\acute et}}$ is finite and faithfully flat: over the complete base the algebra $H$ with reduced fibre splits into local factors with maximal ideal generated by $p$, and over each such factor a nonzero finite free algebra is faithfully flat. It is used in the construction of the formally étale quotient of a Hopf algebra over $\mathcal O$, namely by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_formallyEtale_bialgHom_faithfullyFlat_ker_eq_map_ker_counit_zmodp`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_formallyEtale_bialgHom_faithfullyFlat_ker_eq_map_ker_counit_zmodp).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_RingHom_finite_and_faithfullyFlat_of_isReduced_baseChange_of_injective_zmodp.lean

